    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9563" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">compendĭōsus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		compendium. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Advantageous</i> (opp. damnosus), <i><span class="en">Col. 1, 4,
			5</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Abridged</i>, <i>short</i>, <i>brief</i>, <i>compendious</i>
			(post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">verba,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 11, p. 268, 12</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">iter,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 6</span></i>
			, p. 186, 12: exitus citae mortis, Prud. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεφ</span>. 2, 334.—<i>Adv.</i>:
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">compendĭōsē</span></b> , <i>compendiously</i>, <i>briefly</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Cassiod. Var. 8,
			29</span></i>.—In <i>comp.</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 7, 10</span></i>.</div>
